Package: ENMselect
Type: Package
Title: Evaluate and Select Species Distribution Models Using AUC and MAE
Version: 1.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kamil", "Konowalik", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "kamil.konowalik@gmail.com")
Description: Tools to evaluate and select species distribution models /
    ecological niche models built with any software. Implements the
    simultaneous use of the area under the ROC curve (AUC) and the mean
    absolute error (MAE) proposed in Konowalik and Nosol (2021)
    <doi:10.1038/s41598-020-80062-1>, together with the true skill statistic
    and the continuous Boyce index. Supports spatial block cross-validation
    across folds and background sets, temporal validation of hindcasts against
    dated (e.g. fossil) records matched to the climate of their time, and
    model selection by conventional minimum values or Pareto optimality with a
    tolerance for ties, with bootstrap estimates of selection robustness.
